GEDO STATUE -> TEN-TAILS REVIVAL - PROCEDURE
CLASSIFIED. HANDLER-LEVEL ACCESS.

The Gedo Statue is the husk of the Ten-Tails, emptied when the Sage of Six Paths
divided it into the nine beasts. Restoring it reverses that division.

1. Seal all nine tailed beasts into the Statue, in order, via full ring-bearer
   extraction. Each beast fills one of the nine sealed eyes.
2. With the ninth beast sealed, the Statue's dormant chakra reawakens and the husk
   swells back toward its complete form - the Ten-Tails reborn.
3. A jinchuriki must be prepared to receive and control the revived beast; an
   uncontrolled Ten-Tails is a weapon that turns on its wielder.
4. The controlled Ten-Tails jinchuriki is the vessel for the final technique.

Do not attempt revival with fewer than nine beasts sealed. A partial Statue yields a
partial, ungovernable beast. Patience. All nine, or nothing.
